### 2. Data Cleaning & Transformation (SQL)
All raw data cleaning and heavy aggregation were performed in **[PostgreSQL / MySQL / SQL Server]** before exporting summarized tables to Excel. *(View full scripts in [`/sql_queries`](sql_queries/))*

* **Deduplication & Null Handling:** Removed [X] duplicate records and filtered out [X] rows missing `CustomerID` to ensure accurate user-level tracking.
* **Anomaly Filtering:** Separated canceled transactions (prefixed with `'C'`) into a separate returns table and excluded zero-dollar test entries.
* **Feature Engineering:** Created customer-level **RFM (Recency, Frequency, Monetary)** scores using CTEs and window functions (`NTILE(5)`, `DATEDIFF()`, `LAG()`).

<details>
<summary><b>Click to view sample SQL query (RFM Segmentation)</b></summary>

```sql
WITH customer_metrics AS (
    SELECT 
        customer_id,
        MAX(invoice_date) AS last_purchase_date,
        COUNT(DISTINCT invoice_no) AS frequency,
        SUM(quantity * unit_price) AS monetary_value
    FROM cleaned_transactions
    GROUP BY customer_id
)
SELECT 
    customer_id,
    NTILE(5) OVER (ORDER BY last_purchase_date ASC) AS recency_score,
    NTILE(5) OVER (ORDER BY frequency ASC) AS frequency_score,
    NTILE(5) OVER (ORDER BY monetary_value ASC) AS monetary_score
FROM customer_metrics;
